WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.335
A matching job title is only part of a job search.

2
00:00:03.285 --> 00:00:13.162
Infinity Job Shortlist connects role matching with company financial evidence, helping technology and H R systems jobseekers decide where to look next.

3
00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:17.102
Here is our actual I B M Bob project task.

4
00:00:17.052 --> 00:00:22.236
Bob created the first live shortlist page and connected it to the Python service.

5
00:00:22.236 --> 00:00:26.856
The completed task and its usage are preserved in our public repository.

6
00:00:26.856 --> 00:00:31.427
Later improvements expanded the search and connected the deployed agents.

7
00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:36.393
In the working app, enter H R I S and Python.

8
00:00:36.343 --> 00:00:39.811
Choose a city, a state, or all fifty states.

9
00:00:39.811 --> 00:00:43.389
Focus and experience filters help narrow the search.

10
00:00:43.389 --> 00:00:49.198
Quick search reuses recent evidence, while this option requests a fresh check of employer boards.

11
00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:58.065
Python checks seventy two employer boards and free keyword discovery, normalizes the listings, and retrieves financial evidence.

12
00:00:58.015 --> 00:01:01.974
Bounded parallel requests and caches reduce repeated work.

13
00:01:01.974 --> 00:01:06.373
Collection dates, source failures, and cached results remain visible.

14
00:01:06.373 --> 00:01:09.425
A first search can take longer than a repeat search.

15
00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:14.050
Now the embedded I B M chat reviews the prepared evidence.

16
00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:21.193
Infinity Job Shortlist calls its collaborator, Infinity Company Assessment, with the company financial fields.

17
00:01:21.193 --> 00:01:25.335
The assessment agent explains the supplied score and eligibility.

18
00:01:25.335 --> 00:01:29.992
The shortlist agent then brings the assessments back into the job recommendations.

19
00:01:29.992 --> 00:01:35.629
Short lived signed tokens connect the app without entering an I B M A P I key in the browser.

20
00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:42.100
Review up to ten distinct openings, with financial scores and direct employer links.

21
00:01:42.050 --> 00:01:50.236
Our provisional rubric weights cash flow at fifty percent, growth at thirty percent, and research spending at twenty percent.

22
00:01:50.236 --> 00:01:55.150
Eligibility requires a score above five and positive operating cash flow.

23
00:01:55.150 --> 00:01:58.349
Comparable six month reports can qualify too.

24
00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:04.541
Open the employer's posting and the original financial report to check the evidence yourself.

25
00:02:04.491 --> 00:02:07.003
Missing evidence is marked unassessed.

26
00:02:07.003 --> 00:02:10.851
The score is a research aid, not a guarantee of stability.

27
00:02:10.851 --> 00:02:15.630
The candidate decides whether to apply; the app does not submit applications.

28
00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:21.120
One workflow connects job fit, financial context, and sources.

29
00:02:21.070 --> 00:02:28.484
The code, setup instructions, Bob evidence, and dated tests are available in our public Infinity Project repository.
